# Website / Documentation Site

The documentation site uses Next.js 15 + Fumadocs + React 19 + Tailwind CSS 4.

## Search

Fumadocs requires an explicit API route for search to work. The search route MUST exist:

- **File:** `website/app/api/search/route.ts`
- **Exports:** `{ GET }` created via `createFromSource(source)` from `fumadocs-core/search/server`
- **NEVER** delete this file — search will silently break with no visible errors

If upgrading Fumadocs, verify the `createFromSource` API signature hasn't changed by checking the type definitions in `node_modules/fumadocs-core/dist/search/server.d.ts`.

## Source Configuration

- `website/source.config.ts` — MDX content config
- `website/lib/source.ts` — Fumadocs source loader (imports from `.source/server`)
- Content lives in `/docs` at repo root (not `website/docs`)

## Validation

After any website changes, run `pnpm docs:build` and verify:
1. Build completes without errors
2. `/api/search` appears in the route table output
3. All doc pages are listed under `/docs/[[...slug]]`
